@quill507/dsh-orchestrator-preset README · @quill507/dsh-orchestrator-preset：The repository root **is** the bundle. There is no `bundle/` subdirectory: the files here
are exactly the files that get installed.

---

@quill507/dsh-orchestrator-preset README · Routing sections：The `orch-` prefix itself is not decoration: these skills land in a registry that also holds
whatever else a given machine has installed, so an unprefixed `evidence-protocol` would be a
name waiting to collide.

@quill507/dsh-orchestrator-preset README · How this differs from the upstream aegis pack：aegis supplies **method**: how to write a plan, run strict TDD, debug systematically, run a
review, verify before claiming done. It is a library of skills, and it assumes a single
coordinator doing the work.

@quill507/dsh-orchestrator-preset README · Sourcing: what is upstream, what was measured here：DeepSeek Harness is MIT-licensed: [`github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness`](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness).
Unrelated projects sharing a similar name are not a source for anything in this repository.

---

@quill507/dsh-orchestrator-preset README · Installation：- **At load time, the peers are the barrier.** The host's own loader checks the bundle's
  `peerDependencies` against its own version and, when they do not cover it, **skips the bundle
  whole**:

@quill507/dsh-orchestrator-preset README · Installation：```
  dsh: skipping profile bundle "@quill507/dsh-orchestrator-preset": Error: Plugin @quill507/dsh-orchestrator-preset@0.2.1 is incompatible with dsh 0.2.2-alpha.2: requirements {"@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill-filesystem":"0.2.1-rc.2 || 0.2.1-rc.3","@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools":"0.2.1-rc.2 || 0.2.1-rc.3"}. Running it may cause crashes or data loss. … Exact-version exemption: not active.
  ```

@quill507/dsh-orchestrator-preset README · Installation：`tools/patch-contract.test.mjs` checks the lane gate's `official` lists and the `disabled`
probe against a simulated machine, so a machine-specific name creeping back into any lane's
grant fails loudly rather than at the next delegation.

@quill507/dsh-orchestrator-preset README · 0. Host version gate：**Three barriers, in the order a host meets them: the peers at load, the gate at mount,
`install.sh` only if you use it.** It is worth being precise about which is which, because they
overlap and it is easy to mistake a written-down intention for an enforced one:

@quill507/dsh-orchestrator-preset README · 0. Host version gate：The versions inside those first two bullets: the two dsh packages enumerate the supported set
(`0.2.1-rc.5 || 0.2.2-alpha.2`); `cordis` and `schemastery` enumerate
the two generations the set straddles (`4.0.5 || 4.0.6-alpha.1`, `3.18.5 || 3.18.6-alpha.1`).

@quill507/dsh-orchestrator-preset README · One lane form, and why：**Why there is a `lane-tool-gate` at all.** A preset's `plugins[]` can only **add** plugins;
there is no declarative way to subtract a host tool from a lane. So exclusion cannot be
expressed by the preset mechanism itself — it needs `tools.restrict()`, evaluated along the
calling agent's own scope chain. `lane-tool-gate.mjs` is that gate, mounted inside each lane's
preset.

@quill507/dsh-orchestrator-preset README · (default off, turned on in your own layer — see below).：Restate **both** keys. A patch replaces a row's config rather than deep-merging it, so naming
only the one you are changing drops the other back to its default. A restart is needed either
way: the config is read when the plugin is applied.

@quill507/dsh-orchestrator-preset README · 6. Install the aegis methodology pack：`aegis` is an upstream dependency, not something this repository ships. Install it through
the host, and pin the same released tag in both profiles.

**Turning aegis's automatic injection off, without losing the routing table.**

